================================================================================
Architectural Inspiration, References & Clean-Room Notice
================================================================================

All Rust crates (`plo_cards`, `plo_eval`, `plo_iso`, `plo_range`, `plo_tree`, `plo_cfr`,
`plo_wasm`, `plo_desktop_commands`) and the Tauri 2 / Web UI (`apps/plo_desktop`, `js/`)
were implemented from scratch specifically for 4-card Pot-Limit Omaha (exact 2-hole + 3-board
evaluation, 15-term 4-card inclusion-exclusion terminal counterfactual values, and 2D
equity x nut-blocker postflop bucketing).

We acknowledge the following open-source projects and academic publications whose public
designs, algorithms, and license terms informed our architecture:

1. `wasm-postflop` / `postflop-solver` by b-inary (`https://github.com/b-inary/wasm-postflop`
   and `https://github.com/b-inary/postflop-solver`), distributed under GNU AGPL-3.0:
   - Inspired the browser/WASM + Rust solver crate split and interactive postflop tree
     navigation workflow (note: no Hold'em source code was copied; this repository implements
     PLO-4 4-card combinatorics and 15-term inclusion-exclusion natively).
   - Consistent with our AGPL-3.0-or-later license, any distribution of compiled binaries
     (`.msi`, `.exe`, `.dmg`, `.deb`, `.wasm`) or network-accessible deployment must provide
     access to the complete Corresponding Source under GNU AGPL v3.

2. Discounted Counterfactual Regret Minimization (DCFR):
   - Noam Brown & Tuomas Sandholm, "Solving Imperfect-Information Games via Discounted Regret
     Minimization", AAAI 2019 (`arXiv:1809.04040`).

3. Cactus Kev Prime-Product 5-Card Hand Evaluation:
   - Kevin Suffecool ("Cactus Kev"), prime-product lookup technique for 5-card equivalence
     classes (`7,462` distinct 5-card ranks), adapted here to PLO-4 mandatory 2-hole + 3-board
     evaluation (`crates/plo_eval`).

4. Tauri 2 Application Framework & Dialog Plugin (`https://tauri.app`):
   - Copyright (c) Tauri Programme within The Commons Conservancy, licensed under Apache-2.0
     or MIT (`apps/plo_desktop/src-tauri`).

